# Live scanner notes

When the user reports a live Slack miss, a false alert, late relay, wrong
sw1/sw2/FVG text, or a protocol idea from a live session, append a dated
block to `live/LIVE_SCANNER_NOTES.md` (newest first, below the open
queue). Use the template in that file. Update the open queue if the
note is a repeating pattern.

Do not treat that log as a license to edit tagged OOS `smt_scanner_v8_8.py`
or live `smt_scanner_v8_7.py`. Structural bugs vs the current spec can be
fixed on a feature branch. Protocol changes are a new version. Threshold
retunes to recover one live print must be flagged before any code change.
